@startuml direct-rialto-drm-callback-reentrancy-sequence
title Key-session callbacks versus session teardown (CallbackScope and the running map)

participant "rialto-media-keys-events\nthread" as EV
participant "MediaKeysClient\n(mutex, running, callbackDone)" as MC
participant "RialtoMediaKeySessionAdapter\n(callbacks capture this)" as AD
participant "Teardown thread\n(DrmSessionManager)" as TD
participant "RialtoMediaKeySession" as KS

EV -> MC : onKeyStatusesChanged(id, statuses)
activate MC
MC -> MC : lock mutex; copy callbacks;\nCallbackScope adds this thread to running[id];\nupdate key-status cache; unlock
MC -> AD : onKeyUpdate(...) / onKeysUpdated()\n(no client mutex held)

TD -> AD : delete session -> ~adapter -> clearDecryptContext()
AD -> KS : close() (closeKeySession)
AD -> KS : destruct() (releaseKeySession)
KS -> MC : deregisterSession(id)
MC -> MC : erase callbacks[id], sessions[id]
MC -> MC : wait on callbackDone until running[id]\ncontains no other thread
note right of MC : teardown blocks here\n(untimed) while EV is still\ninside the adapter's callback

AD --> MC : callback returns
MC -> MC : ~CallbackScope: lock, remove this thread\nfrom running[id], notify_all
deactivate MC
MC --> KS : deregisterSession returns
KS --> AD : destruct complete
AD --> TD : adapter memory may now be freed safely

== A callback that deregisters its own session ==
EV -> MC : onLicenseRequest(id) -> callback
MC -> MC : deregisterSession(id) from the same thread
note right of MC : the calling thread is excluded from\nthe wait (onlySelfRunning), so a callback\ncan tear down its own session
MC -> MC : onKeyStatusesChanged: re-check the session is\nstill registered after each onKeyUpdate and before\nonKeysUpdated; stop dispatching the batch if not
@enduml
